  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1200 PM CDT Thu Oct 29 2026\n\nA warm end to the work week proceeds unimpeded with highs around\n80F a good dozen or so degrees over climo norms for this time of\nyear.\n\nThe weekend weather forecast is a little bit wetter with a \nlittle bit better probability of rain, but the overall impact \nweather remains the same. Best wetting occurs between midnight \nSaturday night and midday Sunday, when the bulk of the now storm\ntotal cumulative precipitation of 1/2-1\" amounts over western \nKy occurs; lesser amounts are anticipated to the north and west \nof western Ky.\n\nAfter a brief lull/wane in pops, still daily rain chances carry\non thru next week. The onset of rain chances moves temperatures\nback a little closer to seasonal norms, with lower half 70s\nprevailing for highs this weekend thru next week. The best rain\nchances next week occur Tuesday into Wednesday, with amounts now\nranging from about 1/2 inch in our east, upward to 2 inches \npossibly cumulatively totalling in our west; these projected \namounts have been varying greatly from run-to-run and day-to- \nday, so will be monitored and adjusted accordingly as the event \nnears. For now, the mid week looks like our best chance for \nappreciable rainfall over the broader area that we've had for \nsome time.",
